&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;The Business Systems team defines and builds the business IT architecture that supports the commercial operation of Waymo&#39;s autonomous fleet. The team stands at the intersection of finance, operations and IT; through creative architecture, expertise and attention to detail, it ensures that Waymo has world-class capabilities across all its business processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a strategic and execution-oriented &lt;strong&gt;Digital Engineering Program Lead&lt;/strong&gt; to drive end-to-end transformation across &lt;strong&gt;Supply Chain and Operations&lt;/strong&gt;. This role will lead large-scale digital programs focused on automation, forecasting, planning, global partner integrations, inventory accuracy, logistics efficiency, and operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with Supply Chain, Operations, Finance, Digital Engineering, AI/ML, and cross-functional leaders to translate business needs into scalable systems, drive digital-first capabilities, and ensure successful program delivery from concept to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is ideal for someone who thrives at the intersection of &lt;strong&gt;technology, operations, and program delivery&lt;/strong&gt;—with strong leadership, stakeholder alignment, and execution discipline.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In this hybrid role, you will report to Head of&amp;nbsp; Portfolio Strategy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Leadership &amp;amp; Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the digital transformation for Supply Chain &amp;amp; Operations (planning, logistics, manufacturing, service). Manage end-to-end program delivery: scoping, requirements, execution, and go-live. Define technical/functional plans, risks, and success metrics. Ensure solutions are scalable and align programs with corporate OKRs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Partnership &amp;amp; Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the liaison between Supply Chain/Operations and Digital Engineering. Translate operational needs into system requirements (forecasting, integrations, logistics). Shape digital capabilities for global scaling (automation, AI). Identify gaps for cost/accuracy/throughput optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Engagement &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage cross-functional stakeholders (Finance, Legal, etc.). Run portfolio governance (intake, prioritization, status reviews, executive reporting). Drive alignment on outcomes, timelines, and budget. Present updates to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System &amp;amp; Capability Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own system delivery for: forecasting, partner integrations, inventory, logistics visibility, supplier/vendor management, and work order/service operations. Improve data integrity and operational insights using AI, analytics, and automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget &amp;amp; Vendor Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage program budgets, forecasts, and financial tracking. Oversee vendor partners, SOWs, contracts, and performance, ensuring cost-efficient delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8-10 years of experience in program/project management, digital engineering, or supply chain/operations technology roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educational background - Bachelor of Computer Science or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in supply chain systems, ERP, planning platforms, integrations, logistics, or operations management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading complex, cross-functional technical programs in a fast-growing or enterprise environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent skills in road map planning, stakeholder management, risk mitigation, and executive communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to convert operational pain points into digital solutions with clear business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI/ML, analytics, automation, and data-driven operations preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with digital transformation in global supply chains or operations networks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in autonomous systems, manufacturing operations, hardware supply chain, or fleet operations is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to balance strategy with execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in ambiguity and fast-paced environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
