&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;:4kg&quot; class=&quot;Am aiL Al editable LW-avf tS-tW tS-tY&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Market Entry &amp;amp; Partner Enablement Team consists of Waymo Ops Program Managers focused on enabling the launch and scaling of new market operations end-to-end throughout partners’ (both commercial and validation operators) journeys and across all geographies both internationally and domestically. The team does this by facilitating the integration of new operational partnerships into the Waymo ecosystem. They do this by developing and maintaining processes and documentation for internal use and partner education, and by offering direct support to deal teams leading specialized programs. These programs enable partners to achieve successful, safe, standard-compliant, and independent operations at scale even as Waymo technology, standards, and best practices evolve rapidly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will report to the Manager of New Business Operations - Commercial Growth &amp;amp; Planning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build, maintain, and facilitate the execution of Operations-focused multi-team internal playbooks and documentation to enable successful &amp;amp; reliable international new market launches, covering everything from physical infrastructure and equipment to local vendor relationships and supply chain enablement. You aren&#39;t the expert in any given area, but you take a firm hand to orchestrate, fairly assess risks at all levels, and drive continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify opportunities for process improvement in how Waymo Operations uses to prepare for and execute market entry and early operations expansions in new international cities working closely with internal cross-functional stakeholders across Legal, Regulatory, Safety, Waymo Real Estate, Product, Supply Chain, Business Development and other teams to drive these improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Represent Operations efforts and interests in internal program review cadences focused on market entry from early planning through to commercial launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational Strategy &amp;amp; Program Management Expertise: 7-10+ years of experience in Program Management, specifically in roles focused on Process Excellence, Sales/Ops Enablement, and/or Strategy &amp;amp; Operations. Must have a proven track record of turning ambiguous problems and workflows into clear, actionable decisions, playbooks and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adaptability in High-Growth Environments: Experience working in a fast-paced environment (like Tech or Global Logistics) where products, processes, and standards change frequently. You must be comfortable guiding forward progress with limited information and revisiting plans as the fact base changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-Functional &amp;amp; Leadership Communications Skills: Demonstrated ability to communicate at all levels of an organization and influence without authority, from senior company leaders needing an update to working group subject matter experts needing guidance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with International Launches and/or Global Business Units: Experience program managing or otherwise supporting growth in multi-country business units. You understand that &quot;one size does not fit all&quot; and have a track record of integrating local nuance into a global approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data-Driven Process Improvement: Proficiency in using Lean, Six Sigma, or similar process improvement methodologies to measure the efficacy of a process. You don&#39;t just write a manual; you measure whether that manual actually delivered the desired outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planning and Modeling Experience: Confidence with basic spreadsheet modeling, preferably with physical asset, real estate, and/or headcount planning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30% of the year is spent traveling for in-person time with your team and visiting markets where you are program managing launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$159,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$196,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Waymo Operations exists to deliver the Waymo Driver to the world. We are a global team building and scaling the world&#39;s first and leading autonomous fleet and operations platform. From component sourcing to end customer management, we enable and create value for Waymo through scaled and orchestrated deployment of the Waymo Driver. At Waymo, we are dedicated to building a culture that promotes collaboration and celebration. We value our team members&#39; unique backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences and support and encourage all team members to share their ideas to help Waymo better serve the communities in which we operate. Waymo Operations は、Waymo Driver を世界に届けるための存在です。私たちは、世界初かつ最先端の自律走行車両および運用プラットフォームを構築し、拡大するグローバル チームです。部品調達からエンド カスタマー管理まで、Waymo Driver の大規模かつオーケストレーションされた展開を通じて Waymo の価値を実現し、創造します。Waymo は、協働と称賛を促進する文化の構築に注力しています。チームメンバーの独自の背景、視点、経験を重視し、Waymo が事業を展開するコミュニティにさらに貢献できるよう、すべてのチームメンバーがアイデアを共有することをサポートし、奨励しています。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;日本のオペレーション リードは、日本全域における Waymo オペレーションの戦略的方向性と日々の業務遂行の責任を担う上級幹部です。このリーダーは、Waymo のグローバル ビジョンを規律あるローカル戦略へと落とし込み、自動運転車の安全かつ信頼性の高い大規模展開を実現します。地域における Waymo Operations の主要代表として、規制当局やパートナーとの重要な関係を管理するとともに、複雑なマルチ マーケット環境におけるオペレーションの卓越性を推進します。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Japan Operations Lead&lt;/strong&gt; is the senior executive responsible for the strategic direction and daily execution of Waymo’s operations across Japan. This leader translates Waymo’s global vision into a disciplined local strategy, ensuring the safe and reliable deployment of autonomous vehicles at scale. As the primary representative for Waymo Operations in the region, they manage key relationships with regulators and partners while driving operational excellence across complex, multi-market environments&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;このハイブリッドな役割では、配車サービス事業（Ride-Hail Operations）の責任者にレポートします。&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In this hybrid role, you will report to the Head of Ride Hail Operations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;業務内容:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;戦略の実行: Waymo の長期目標および拡張ロードマップに沿って、日本における運用戦略を策定および実行します, &lt;strong&gt;Execute Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and execute the operational strategy for Japan, aligned with Waymo’s long-term objectives and expansion roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;安全パフォーマンスの維持: 地域における安全パフォーマンス、サービスの信頼性、顧客からの信頼、運用の健全性に対して、エンドツーエンドの責任を担います。&lt;strong&gt;Maintain Safety Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain end-to-end accountability for regional safety performance, service reliability, customer trust, and operational health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;市場参入の主導: 市場参入および事業拡大の取り組みを主導し、立ち上げから規模拡大まで、運用準備、パートナーの能力、実行規律を確保します。&lt;strong&gt;Lead Market Entry:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead market entry and expansion initiatives, ensuring operational readiness, partner capability, and execution discipline from launch through scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;戦略的関係の構築: Waymo の上級代表として、コミュニティ リーダー、規制当局、戦略的パートナーとの強固な関係を構築します。&lt;strong&gt;Build Strategic Relationships:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the senior representative for Waymo, building strong relationships with community leaders, regulators, and strategic partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;運用上の優先順位の確立: すべての APAC 市場において、明確な運用上の優先順位、パフォーマンス目標、ガバナンス体制を確立します。&lt;strong&gt;Establish Operating Priorities:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish clear operating priorities, performance expectations, and governance structures across all APAC markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;パートナーのパフォーマンス向上: パートナーおよびベンダーのパフォーマンス向上を推進し、基準の設定、成果のモニタリング、継続的改善を実現します。&lt;strong&gt;Drive Partner Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive partner and vendor performance, setting standards, monitoring outcomes, and enabling continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;地域チームの統合: オペレーション、安全、プロダクト、エンジニアリング、エンタープライズ チーム全体における地域統合の中心的役割を担います。&lt;strong&gt;Integrate Regional Teams:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the regional point of integration across operations, safety, product, engineering, and enterprise teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;予算管理: 予算計画、コスト管理、運用効率の確保に関する責任を担います。&lt;strong&gt;Own Budget Oversight:&lt;/strong&gt; Own budget planning, cost control, and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;リーダーシップ人材の育成: 地域のリーダーシップ人材を採用、指導、育成し、説明責任、主体性、卓越した実行力を重視する文化を育みます。&lt;strong&gt;Develop Leadership Talent:&lt;/strong&gt; Build, lead, and develop regional leadership talent, fostering a culture of accountability, ownership, and execution excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;企業戦略への影響: Waymo 内で日本の事業および市場の声を代表し、企業戦略や投資判断に影響を与えます。&lt;strong&gt;Influence Enterprise Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Represent the voice of Japanese operations and markets within Waymo, influencing enterprise strategy and investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have: 必須条件:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;地域オペレーション、テクノロジー、または物流分野における 10 年以上の上級リーダーシップ経験 15+ years of senior leadership experience in regional operations, tech, or logistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;日本における市場参入および事業拡大の実績 Proven success in market entry and scaling operations across Japan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;安全性が重要な環境の管理経験 Experience managing safety-critical environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;規制当局対応および戦略的パートナー管理に関する豊富な経験 Strong background in regulatory engagement and strategic partner management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ガバナンス、KPI、運用上の優先順位の確立に関する専門知識 Expertise in establishing governance, KPIs, and operational priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;エンジニアリング チームと現場チーム間の部門横断的連携を推進する能力 Skilled in cross-functional integration between engineering and field teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;優れたチームの構築およびリーダーシップ人材育成の実績 Proficiency in P&amp;amp;L management, budget planning, and cost control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;企業レベルの戦略および投資判断に影響を与える能力 Track record of building high-performing teams and developing leadership talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;歓迎条件:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AV / フリート運用の経験 Experience in AV / Fleet Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;損益管理（P&amp;amp;L）、予算計画、コスト管理に関する高い専門性 High expertise in P&amp;amp;L management, budget planning, and cost control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel 出張要件:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;年に 2～3 回、MTV / 本社への出張が可能であることTravel - 1 per QTR to head quarters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Waymo Operations exists to deliver the Waymo Driver to the world. We are a global team building and scaling the world&#39;s first and leading autonomous fleet and operations platform. From component sourcing to end customer management, we enable and create value for Waymo through scaled and orchestrated deployment of the Waymo Driver. At Waymo, we are dedicated to building a culture that promotes collaboration and celebration. We value our team members&#39; unique backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences and support and encourage all team members to share their ideas to help Waymo better serve the communities in which we operate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In this onsite role, you will report to a Fleet Readiness Sr. Lead&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead as a Technical SME: Act as the primary technical expert for fleet operations, providing in-depth knowledge and troubleshooting support to address complex vehicle issues outside of documented standard operating procedures. Engage with Waymo Engineering teams and work directly with OEM partners to resolve SDS-Ready faults.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Real-time Support: Offer immediate support to resolve technical challenges in both owned-and-operated and partner-led depots, ensuring minimal downtime and operational continuity. Required to travel to partner-led depots and provide in person support.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer Training &amp;amp; Training development SME: Administer on-the-job training (including train-the-trainer) to operational teams as a certified instructor, enhancing their technical skills and enabling them to address recurring issues effectively.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align with Vendors: Collaborate with vendors to address technical concerns, ensuring alignment with Waymo&#39;s standards and fostering a culture of accountability and continuous learning.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document Technical Knowledge: Develop and maintain technical documentation, troubleshooting guides, and best practices to support operational teams and improve overall fleet health.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively Identify Risks: Provide expertise to improve preventive maintenance practices, collaborate with engineering teams to assist in identifying and address potential issues before they impact fleet performance. Maintain the latest knowledge on all product releases and their impacts to fleet performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years experience in technician or mechanical engineering role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of technical and tooling mechanisms in fleet operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability works hands-on with equipment, machinery, or systems, performing maintenance, troubleshooting, repairs, and installations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in managing multiple projects simultaneously while ensuring timely delivery and quality outcomes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with cross-functional teams, external partners and executives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience diagnosing &amp;amp; repairing Electric Vehicles, &amp;amp; ability to diagnose low voltage electrical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication &amp;amp; collaborations: Effective communications skills to collaborate across teams &amp;amp; clearly document knowledge for cross-market knowledge-sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitating change: Change management principles, lead training sessions, problem solving &amp;amp; decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Skills: Proficiency in leveraging tools, technology and ability to troubleshoot and resolve complex technical issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem Identification &amp;amp; Resolution: Proactively identifying potential challenges, planning remediation steps &amp;amp; risk mitigation strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process Improvement: Proactively identify process improvement opportunities &amp;amp; executing strategies to improve processes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of Electric Vehicles, with integrated AV systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience diagnosing or repairing High Voltage propulsion systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Requirement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing and able to travel on short notice to support fleet needs - could be up to 25% of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The expected hourly range for this position is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level.&amp;nbsp; Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Hourly Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$60.10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$62.99 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Waymo Operations は、Waymo Driver を世界に届けるための存在です。私たちは、世界初かつ最先端の自律走行車両および運用プラットフォームを構築し、拡大するグローバル チームです。部品調達からエンド カスタマー管理まで、Waymo Driver の大規模かつオーケストレーションされた展開を通じて Waymo の価値を実現し、創造します。Waymo は、協働と称賛を促進する文化の構築に注力しています。チームメンバーの独自の背景、視点、経験を重視し、Waymo が事業を展開するコミュニティにさらに貢献できるよう、すべてのチームメンバーによるアイデアの共有をサポートし、奨励しています。Waymo Operations exists to deliver the Waymo Driver to the world. We are a global team building and scaling the world&#39;s first and leading autonomous fleet and operations platform. From component sourcing to end customer management, we enable and create value for Waymo through scaled and orchestrated deployment of the Waymo Driver. At Waymo, we are dedicated to building a culture that promotes collaboration and celebration. We value our team members&#39; unique backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences and support and encourage all team members to share their ideas to help Waymo better serve the communities in which we operate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;フリート開発およびサービス品質責任者&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;の直属として、こうしたハイブリッドな役割を担っていただきます。&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In this hybrid role, you will report to Head of Fleet Development &amp;amp; Service Quality.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will: 業務内容&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Leverage in-depth knowledge and troubleshooting expertise to address complex issues outside of documented standard operating procedures. Engage with Waymo Engineering teams and OEM partners to resolve concerns;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;技術エキスパートとして主導的役割を果たす:&lt;/strong&gt; 豊富な知識とトラブルシューティングの専門知識を活用して、標準操作手順で規定されていない複雑な問題に対処します。Waymo エンジニアリング チームおよび相手先ブランド製造パートナーと協力し、懸念事項を解決します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimize vehicle downtime by managing escalations from partner technicians facing novel or complex issues. Guide these diagnostics remotely and in-person; &lt;strong&gt;パートナー サポートを提供する:&lt;/strong&gt; 新たな問題や複雑な問題に直面しているパートナー技術者からのエスカレーションに対応し、車両のダウンタイムを最小限に抑えます。リモートと対面の両方で問題の診断をサポートします。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct on-the-job training (including train-the-trainer) to fleet service teams as a certified instructor. Assist in the continuous development of training content; &lt;strong&gt;トレーニングの実施と開発を行う:&lt;/strong&gt; 認定インストラクターとして、フリート サービス チームへの実地研修（トレーナーのトレーニングを含む）を実施します。また、トレーニング コンテンツの継続的な開発を支援します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure market adherence to service and quality assurance standards that drive safety and consistency. Conduct regular audits and assessments to verify compliance;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;品質基準を維持する:&lt;/strong&gt; 安全性と一貫性を推進するサービスおよび品質保証基準が市場で確実に遵守されるようにします。コンプライアンスを確認するために定期的な監査と評価を実施します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering teams to identify and address potential issues before they impact fleet uptime. Perform analysis that identifies high value diagnostic development opportunities;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;技術知識を文書化する:&lt;/strong&gt; フリート サービス チームをサポートするための技術ドキュメント、トラブルシューティング ガイド、操作手順、ベスト プラクティスを開発および管理します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain technical documentation, troubleshooting guides, operating procedures, and best practices to support fleet service teams; &lt;strong&gt;リスクと機会を積極的に特定する:&lt;/strong&gt; エンジニアリング チームと連携して、フリートの稼働時間に影響が出る前に潜在的な問題を特定し、対処します。また、価値の高い診断開発の機会を特定するための分析を実施します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have: 必須条件:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilingual - competent speaking and writing both Japanese and English; バイリンガル - 日本語と英語の両方で会話と文章作成が可能な方&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years experience in an automotive technician or automotive engineering role;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;自動車整備士または自動車エンジニアリング職で 5 年以上の経験を有している方&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mastery of automotive diagnostic strategies, service methods, and tools covering electrical, including high voltage powertrains, mechanical, and networking (e.g. CAN),&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
