&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As part of Waymo&#39;s Legal team, you will work on the exciting legal issues surrounding our transformational autonomous driving technology and help drive our business lines forward from technology ideation through scaled commercial deployment.&amp;nbsp; We partner with our public policy, safety, security and privacy experts to define transportation policy for the autonomous driving world to come, advising on regulatory changes that support and protect our users around the world.&amp;nbsp; We collaborate with our engineering, product, strategy and operations teams to develop and protect our intellectual property portfolio and drive our corporate and commercial transactions. We ensure compliance with an increasingly complex and dynamic range of global regulations. And we anticipate, mitigate, and litigate high-profile and precedent-setting legal matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Waymo の法務チームの一員として、Waymo の革新的な自動運転技術を取り巻く興味深い法的問題に取り組み、技術構想から大規模な商用展開まで、Waymo の事業部門の推進に貢献していただきます。Waymo は、公共政策、安全、セキュリティ、プライバシーの専門家と提携して、将来の自動運転の世界における交通政策を定義し、世界中のユーザーをサポートし保護する規制の改正について助言します。エンジニアリング、製品、戦略、運用の各チームと連携して、知的財産ポートフォリオを開発、保護し、企業取引および商取引を推進しています。ますます複雑化し、変化し続ける世界的な規制への準拠を保証します。また、注目度が高く先例となるような法的問題を予測して軽減し、訴訟を起こします&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this hybrid role you will report directly to our Senior Program Manager, Regulatory Compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;レギュラトリー・コンプライアンス担当シニア・プログラム・マネージャーの直属として、こうしたハイブリッドな役割を担っていただきます。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will / 業務内容:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with legal counsel to intake and document regulatory compliance requirements for Waymo, its vendors, and partners, with a primary focus on the APAC region. This includes creating an inventory and mapping of requirements in a centralized tool/repository, communicating requirements to stakeholders, and evaluating the sufficiency of proposed compliance activities. / 弁護士と連携し、Waymo、そのベンダー、パートナーの規制遵守要件を収集し、文書化します（主にアジア太平洋地域を担当）。これには、中央管理ツール / リポジトリにおける要件のリスト作成とマッピング、関係者への要件の通知、提案されたコンプライアンス活動の妥当性評価が含まれます。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and operate a communication strategy with xfn partners to support efficient and effective change management for net new and changing requirements. / クロスファンクショナル パートナーとのコミュニケーション戦略を定義、運用し、新規要件や要件変更に伴う効率的かつ効果的なチェンジ マネジメントを支援します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help ensure appropriate program governance for new markets and maintenance for existing markets - incl. the drafting and management of policies, standards, SOPs, and training documents in accordance with Waymo’s documentation policies and systems. / 新規市場における適切なプログラム ガバナンスの確保と、既存市場におけるプログラムの維持管理を支援します。これには、Waymo の文書管理ポリシーとシステムに準拠した、ポリシー、規格、標準作業手順、トレーニング文書の作成と管理が含まれます。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build risk assessments and develop evaluation metrics in partnership with other members of the AV Compliance team. / AV コンプライアンス チームの他のメンバーと協力して、リスク評価を構築し、評価指標を策定します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employ the use of automation via Gemini or other systems as much as possible, including the creation of requirements and drafting of policies and communication documents. / 要件の定義、ポリシーやコミュニケーション文書の作成などにおいて、Gemini やその他のシステムを活用し、自動化を可能な限り推進します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have / 必要な条件/経験:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Core experience evaluating and tracking regulatory requirements, ideally within a GRC tool or a similar system, including a demonstrable history of writing policies, standards, or other documentation to support xfn governance efforts. / できれば GRC ツールまたは類似のシステムを用いた、規制要件の評価と管理を中心とする実務経験。部門横断的なガバナンス活動を支援するためのポリシー、規格、その他の文書を作成した実績があること。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing communication strategies to facilitate change management, ensuring effective, consistent, and efficient information dissemination to key stakeholders. / チェンジ マネジメントを促進するためのコミュニケーション戦略の策定、実行経験。主要な関係者に対し、情報を効果的、効率的に一貫性を持って伝達できること。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to speak and write in both Japanese and English fluently / 日本語と英語の両方で流暢に会話と読み書きができる能力&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly collaborative, creative, and organized, with action-oriented problem solving skills. / 協調性、創造性、計画性に優れ、行動志向型の問題解決能力を備えていること。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrable instinct and bias to automate processes and use AI where possible. / 可能な限りプロセスを自動化し、AI を活用しようとする、実績に裏打ちされた鋭い感覚と志向を持っていること。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer / 望ましい経験/スキル:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience assembling, managing, and communicating regulatory requirements to stakeholders in a highly dynamic, fast-paced, and often ambiguous environment / 変化が激しく、ペースが速く、不透明な環境において、規制要件を整理、管理し、関係者に伝達してきた経験&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to roll up your sleeves and do what needs to be done, and ability to conceptualize and operationalize of new processes that improve and/or close gaps in existing flows, with a bias toward automating as much as possible / 自ら行動することをいとわず、必要なことを成し遂げる意欲。既存のフローの改善や不備の解消のために新しいプロセスを概念化、運用化する能力。可能な限り自動化を優先する姿勢&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrably strong project and program management skills / プロジェクト管理やプログラム管理において実証済みの高度なスキル&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High EQ with personally responsible, team player mentality / 高い EQ、責任感、チーム プレーヤーとしての精神&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Jira user; highly familiar with its capabilities and shortcomings / Jira を積極的に利用しており、その機能と欠点を熟知していること&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of regulatory environments in other APAC countries / 日本以外のアジア太平洋地域における規制環境に関する知識&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Travel Requirements / 出張要件:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to CA 1-2x per year for team/company events / チームや会社主催のイベントのため、カリフォルニア州へ年1〜2回程度の出張があります。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;The Regional Ops &amp;amp; Compliance - Market Entry senior program manager functions as the primary integration point for new international market entry, aligning global strategy with local execution requirements. This role serves as the authoritative lead for the international market or region, responsible for synthesizing complex inputs from operations, product, policy, and safety teams to ensure a unified launch. By acting as the single source of truth during the activation phase, this lead navigates dynamic regulatory environments and community nuances to translate local realities into actionable insights for global cross-functional and leadership teams. The core objective is to drive mission-critical readiness milestones and provide a clear framework for escalation and resolution, ensuring a seamless transition from initial market bring-up to stable, long-term commercial operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate Regional Workstreams: Lead daily synchronization between global engineering and local operational teams to ensure infrastructure, depot readiness, and vehicle deployment hit critical milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the Regional Integration Point: Serve as the primary &quot;bridge&quot; between central product/policy teams and local realities, synthesizing complex regional nuances into actionable project plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Regulatory &amp;amp; Compliance Readiness: Manage the end-to-end permit lifecycle and audit operational logs to ensure 100% adherence to municipal requirements and European safety standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve Execution Bottlenecks: Function as the chief escalation point for local authorities and internal stakeholders, proactively unblocking technical or bureaucratic hurdles during the bring-up phase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivate Local Ecosystems: Build strategic partnerships with emergency services, transit authorities, and community leaders to ensure safe integration and a positive public perception of the service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure Operational Stability: Oversee the transition from pilot testing to full commercial scaling, ensuring local feedback is integrated into the global product roadmap for long-term viability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 10+ years of experience in market expansion, operations management, or complex program leadership, specifically within the mobility, autonomous vehicle, or high-growth tech sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 3 years of experience in Operations or Management Consulting practices, handling fast scaling clients and complex project management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in leading cycles of international market entries or large-scale operational rollouts within highly regulated urban environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to navigate complex European regulatory frameworks and a track record of maintaining strategic relationships with municipal transport authorities or government bodies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with the ability to translate technical engineering constraints and operational risks into concise briefings for C-suite leadership and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced data synthesis skills, with a measurable ability to convert operational metrics, local feedback, and pilot data into technical product requirements and actionable scaling plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading go to market or operational scaling projects in top management consulting firms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience in the Autonomous Vehicle sector, with a deep understanding of L4 technology and the specific safety standards required for driverless commercial operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience managing the physical and logistical requirements of urban infrastructure, such as depot mobilization, fleet deployment, or site readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Product Fluency: Ability to engage deeply with engineering and product teams to translate complex AV sensor limitations or infrastructure requirements into local operational playbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure &amp;amp; Depot Mobilization: Background in overseeing the physical setup of high-tech depots or electric vehicle (EV) charging hubs, including site selection and hardware installation oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder Diplomacy: Advanced experience in public-sector engagement, specifically in educating local emergency services and transit authorities on the nuances of interacting with autonomous fleets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level.&amp;nbsp; Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£118,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£124,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

